<section id="companion-try" class="fc-try" aria-labelledby="companion-try-title"><div class="fr-wrap fr-section"><div class="fc-try-heading"><h2 id="companion-try-title">A little prayer. <br/> A way to join in.</h2><p>You can begin here before printing. Anyone may name an intention, keep it quietly, or simply listen.</p></div><ol class="fc-steps"><li><h3>Choose a mystery.</h3><p>For a first moment together, think about the Annunciation: the angel Gabriel brings Mary the news that she will be the mother of Jesus. You can also choose another mystery from the <a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/how-to-pray-the-rosary/#mysteries' ) ); ?>">four sets of mysteries</a>.</p><p class="fc-note">Scripture reference: Luke 1:26–38.</p></li><li><h3>Follow a bead.</h3><p>With a printed companion, children can trace names and color beads as the family prays. Without a printout, point to a bead on the <a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/how-to-pray-the-rosary/#guided-prayer' ) ); ?>">guided Rosary</a> or follow the words below.</p></li><li><h3>Let a child lead.</h3><p>Invite someone to begin one Hail Mary and let others answer. Reading, responding and quiet listening are all ways to take part.</p></li></ol><div class="fc-prayer" aria-labelledby="fc-hail-title"><h3 id="fc-hail-title">Pray one Hail Mary together.</h3><p>Hail Mary, full of grace, the Lord is with thee. Blessed art thou among women, and blessed is the fruit of thy womb, Jesus. Holy Mary, Mother of God, pray for us sinners, now and at the hour of our death. Amen.</p><a class="text-link" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/how-to-pray-the-rosary/#guided-prayer' ) ); ?>">Continue with the complete guided Rosary</a></div></div></section>
